 ## Overview
-The Emission-Absorption Model is the standard optical model for direct volume rendering, computing the final radiance reaching the eye by integrating light emitted by a participating medium along a ray, attenuated by the medium's absorption [S1, S2, S3, S8, unofficial]. It solves the problem of determining visible radiance from a 3D scalar field representing a participating medium by modeling the volume as filled with small light-emitting particles described by a density function, rather than modeling them individually [S2, S12, unofficial]. Unlike its parent [Emission-only Model](1016-emission-only-model.md), which only adds intensity, this model accounts for both light addition (emission) and light blocking (absorption/occlusion), allowing for the distinction of depth order along the ray [S19, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from full radiative transfer models by completely ignoring scattering, which maintains interactivity while providing a high level of realism for phenomena like clouds, smoke, and opaque surfaces in NeRFs [S3, S17, unofficial].
+The Emission-Absorption Model is the standard optical model for direct volume rendering, computing the final radiance reaching the eye by integrating light emitted by a participating medium along a ray, attenuated by the medium's absorption [S1, S2, S3, S8, unofficial]. It solves the problem of determining visible radiance from a 3D scalar field representing a participating medium by modeling the volume as filled with small light-emitting particles described by a density function, rather than modeling them individually [S2, unofficial][S12]. Unlike its parent [Emission-only Model](1016-emission-only-model.md), which only adds intensity, this model accounts for both light addition (emission) and light blocking (absorption/occlusion), allowing for the distinction of depth order along the ray [S19, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from full radiative transfer models by completely ignoring scattering, which maintains interactivity while providing a high level of realism for phenomena like clouds, smoke, and opaque surfaces in NeRFs [S3, unofficial][S17].
 
